        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "096100b0-b78f-59f5-8321-66533236719e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nikita Khrushchev\n- Places: Soviet Union, Albania, Yugoslavia, Eastern Bloc\n- Events: Soviet–Albanian split\n- Concepts: de-Stalinization, Secret Speech, rapprochement, Soviet space program, domestic policy reforms\n\nFacts:\n- The Soviet–Albanian split was the worsening of relations between the Soviet Union and Albania during 1955–1961.\n- Nikita Khrushchev's rapprochement with Yugoslavia contributed to the Soviet–Albanian split.\n- Nikita Khrushchev's Secret Speech and subsequent de-Stalinization policies contributed to the Soviet–Albanian split.\n- Soviet efforts to extend de-Stalinization into Albania, as in other Eastern Bloc states, contributed to the Soviet–Albanian split.\n- Nikita Khrushchev was responsible for de-Stalinization in the Soviet Union.\n- Nikita Khrushchev backed the progress of the early Soviet space program.\n- Nikita Khrushchev introduced several relatively liberal reforms in Soviet domestic policy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
